# shell: desktop
# PVL-070: a band that grows over one more row repaints that row, not the
# listing.  The difference region has been computed since the repaint helper
# was written; nothing consumed it.
wait 8
note the sweep starts BELOW the rows, in empty window, and grows upward
press 200 280
move 200 137
wait 6
note it covers the last two rows now
draw-reset
note grown by exactly one row's height: the row it grew OVER is painted
note again, and the two it already covered are not -- a band that damaged
note its whole rectangle would paint every row it covers
move 200 117
wait 6
expect-drawn 2
expect-drawn at-least 1
release 200 172
note and the window as a whole is what a full redraw would draw
expect-same-as-redraw
note a sweep over the empty ground below the rows leaves nothing of itself
note behind either
wait 8
press 100 280
move 300 240
release 300 240
wait 20
expect-same-as-redraw
quit
